# DHI-11 V5 stock reconciliation — 2026-09-05

Outcome: all 23 planned raw-stock transfers bind uniquely. **109 PASS / 36 WARN / 0 FAIL / 1 SKIP; overall WARN; release HOLD.** The formula has not been compounded or smelled. Neither the ingredient list nor a dose was changed in this step. The 30 mL card still contains 6,000 µL of raw stocks plus 24,000 µL ethanol 96%; the 15 mL card is exactly half. Irotyl remains absent and no ingredient-count cap was imposed.

## Evidence and implementation scope

The literature-first and verification skills kept this step local and receipt-led: no new chemical-property assertions or external model calls. Canonical user-correction records had already established the five stocks, but c4d5 used a different inventory lineage. No generic successor writer exists; the existing dated-successor validator in `engine/inventory_parser.py` was extended narrowly. No pipeline script was created.

The new head is `data/governance/inventory_user_authority_overlay_20260905_reconciled.json`, normalized SHA-256 `6b484bb4bfe2be531026d9fda3422d587bdff76f3a4758348b1453d63b1ea170`. Its parent remains the unchanged c4d5 September 4 `_002` overlay, SHA-256 `e24ecddb690760a1f0d545855ba93c4d60680ebd83c9585d60e4e36ae2f7ce09`.

Byte-identical copies of the canonical source receipts are in `data/governance/evidence/`. Their hashes are `e2fe66cb8077da38142913a73b0d77acd14b6e4953f6155bb2011e1e2bb851a4` (September 4) and `08d0f0e41f90741200b3e915789ddd044cbbf7b0ce1b1aa266053452781bb17f` (September 5). Only the explicitly selected records are imported. Canonical September 4 IDs collide with different materials in c4d5, so new local IDs preserve source-record provenance without conflating the chains.

